            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "SGB (Sovereign Gold Bond) 2023-24 scheme Series IV subscription will be start from 12th - 16th February, 2024. Date of Issuance - 21st February, 2024."
            }
          },{
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Is it mandatory to redeem SGB after 8 years?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Though the tenor of the bond is 8 years, early encashment/redemption of the bond is allowed after fifth year from the date of issue on coupon payment dates. The bond will be tradable on Exchanges, if held in demat form."
            }
          }, {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can I exit SGB before 5 years?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Although the (SGB) Sovereign Gold Bond has a tenor of 8 years, it can be redeemed prematurely on coupon payment dates after the 5th year from the date of issue. A charge of ₹150 + 18% GST will be imposed for rematerialisation or redemption."
            }
          }]
